From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:24:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: a frame packing card for 3D TVs and
 projectors

Whether a PC sends HDMI 3D frame packing is found only by playing a 3D
film today (issue 33: NVIDIA refused it; a user with four NVIDIA cards
saw it for a few seconds and then side by side). The check gets a card
of its own, "3D: frame packing", where a display connected says in its
EDID that it takes 3D (3D_present in its HDMI vendor block, HDMI 1.4b
8.3.2; every such display takes frame packing at 1080p24):

- it plays the 3D clip of hades-check (hades-check-3d-sbs.mkv: the
  SDR card for each eye, half side by side, 1080p at 24000/1001, its
  Matroska StereoMode set), with Kodi's 3D settings as it needs them:
  3D played in the preferred mode, that mode the same as the video,
  the refresh rate following the video where it does not at all. Only
  those that are not so already are changed, with the journal of the
  check, and every one is put back after (hades-check-restore puts
  them back before Kodi starts again if it stops in the middle);
- it reads what the player information says of the 3D output while
  the clip plays (hades.out.stereo, hades.out.mode), and why frame
  packing was not used where it was not: Kodi's lines in kodi.log
  ("3D output: frame packing is not used: ...") and the driver's in
  the kernel log ("Hades: HDMI 3D frame packing refused: ...", the
  lines that nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9084 adds);
- it asks how the TV showed it (in 3D, two halves, no picture), and
  says it all: frame packing taken and its mode, or what the video
  went out as and why. The summary of the check, which a diagnostic
  report carries, has one line of it.

Without a display that takes 3D the card says so and plays nothing;
"Everything" leaves it out then. With the 3D output of Hades off
("Switch the display to 3D (HDMI)") it says that setting.

The A/B comparison's way of setting settings back (journal first,
read back, journal removed) is now apply_values(), which both use.

Strings 33850 to 33869 (33857 not used), in English, es_es, es_ar
and es_mx.
